# Components

How a governance rule reaches a target project.

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  accTitle: Governance components
  accDescr: A rule catalog feeds an installer, which writes into a target project.
  A["Rule catalog"] --> B["Installer"]
  B --> C["Target project"]
```

The installer at `src/gov/install.ts` reads the catalog and writes each rule into the target's own folder. Nothing in the catalog is copied by hand, so a rule added upstream reaches every project on the next install.

Drift is a separate path. `src/gov/sync.ts` compares an installed copy against the catalog and reports what diverged rather than overwriting it, which keeps a project's local edits from disappearing on an update.
